<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n85750" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πορθμ-εύω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>carry</i> or <i>ferry over</i> a strait, river, etc., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στρατόν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Rh.</u>
					429
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινὰς εἰς Σαλαμῖνα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aeschin.
					3.158
				</span></i>
			: then, generally, <i>carry over, carry,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐφετμὰς τάσδε πόρθμευσον πάλιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ch.</u>
					685
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δεῦρο π. βρέφος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Ion</u>
					1599
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γραφὰς πρὸς Ἄργος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>IT</u>
					735
				</span></i>
			; also, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π.τιϝὰ ἐκ γῆς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Tr.</u>
					802
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>IT</u>
				1358
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. πόδα, ἴχνος,</span>
			<i>advance,</i> ib.<i><span class="en">
				936
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				266
			</span></i>: metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰς δάκρυα π. ὑπομνήσει κακῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Or.</u>
					1032
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινὰ εἰς αἱματηρὸν γάμον δόλῳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>IT</u>
					371
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποῖ διωγμὸν πορθμεύεις;</span>
			how far <i>dost thou carry</i> it? ib.<i><span class="en">
				1435
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀχέρων ἄχεα π. βροτοῖσιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Licymn.
					2
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πορθμεύει γὰρ ἔμοιγε κύλιξ παρὰ σοῦ
					τὸ φίλημα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					5.260
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Agath.
			</span></i>):—
				Pass.
			, <i>to be carried</i> or <i>ferried over from place to
				place,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				2.97
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπ᾽ ὄχοις π.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Tr.</u>
					569
				</span></i>
			(anap.): c.acc. loci, <i>pass over</i> or <i>through,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λευκὴν αἰθέρα πορθμευόμενος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Andr.</u>
					1229
				</span></i>
			(anap.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Act.
			intr., <i>pass over,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποταμούς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Ax.</u>
					371c
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀχέροντος ὕδωρ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					7.68
				</span></i>
			(<i><span class="en">
				Arch.
			</span></i>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κύματα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Epigr.Gr.</u>
					522.1
				</span></i>
			(<span class="entity">Thessalonica</span>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τίς ἀστὴρ ὅδε π.;</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>IA</u>
					6
				</span></i>
			(anap.).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
